        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel shuts down following war flare-up with Iran Middle East Issued on: 08/06/2026 - 16:46 Iran and Israel say they've now halted attacks, after their first exchange of fire since a ceasefire in April. US President Donald Trump told them to stop fighting, as Israel reported 30 missiles from Israel and Israel struck back. Among ordinary Israelis, it stoked of a return to full-blown war. Lebanese 'stuck between a rock and a hard place' as Israel strikes south of country 08/06/2026 Middle East Iran halts strikes against Israel, Netanyahu stuck between Trump and ministers 08/06/2026 Middle East Despite tension over war flare-up, fallout between Trump and Netanyahu unlikely 08/06/2026 Middle East Israel, Iran trade fire in first clash since truce 08/06/2026 Middle East Tension rises between Israel and the US amid flare-up with Iran 08/06/2026 Middle East Lebanon 'a playground for others': fresh strikes on Beirut trigger concern 08/06/2026 Middle East In Lebanon, temporary cemeteries house the dead exiled by the war 08/06/2026 Middle East Hostilities escalate between Iran and Israel in blow to truce 08/06/2026 Middle East Israel, Iran trade strikes for first time since truce in 'self-created nightmare for Trump' 08/06/2026 Middle East"
